  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_018, a multimodal multiprofile model using PCA RNA, ResNet50 images, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion, with validation accuracy 0.619 and F1 0.610. This suggests the current best design direction, but it is unclear whether concat fusion is specifically responsible or whether weighted fusion could improve calibration of the modalities. config_019 changes only fusion from concat to weighted while keeping all other settings fixed, directly isolating the fusion effect. Under a limited budget, this is a high-value exploitation step because it tests a logical extension of the best known configuration and clarifies whether fusion strategy is an important design choice before moving to larger changes such as new image encoders or RNA encoders."
}

